text When this specification requires a user agent to  representing a particular time (which could be the special value Not-a-Number), the milliseconds component of that time, if any, must be truncated to an integer, and the time value of the newly created  object must represent the resulting truncated time.
text create a Date object
link Date https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-date-objects
text "For instance, given the time 23045 millionths of a second after 01:00 UTC on January 1st 2000, i.e. the time 2000-01-01T00:00:00.023045Z, then the  object created representing that time would represent the same time as that created representing the time 2000-01-01T00:00:00.023Z, 45 millionths earlier. If the given time is NaN, then the result is a  object that represents a time value NaN (indicating that the object does not represent a specific instant of time)."
